WEBVTT

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:15.360
"I can't overcome it"  "I'm annoyed"

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:20.100
Even if I break down those hurdles

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:28.310
No answer emerges

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:34.810
Am I being controlled?  Everyone on the field

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:39.750
Isn't scared, go away, but...

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:43.450
The unseen road to the future

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:51.200
Cannot be chosen

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:54.500
Close your eyes and cut with your heart

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:58.160
just like cards, surely

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:03.230
It was promised  yes!  you are the winner

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:06.100
never lose!  Cut with your heart

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.330
just like cards, surely

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:16.680
Because a miracle will occur

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:26.400
Fire the ectoplasm!

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:42.040
Magician's Student
Dark Magician Girl

00:01:46.970 --> 00:01:54.100
Dark Magician, I won't let your self-sacrifice go to waste!

00:01:55.920 --> 00:02:00.480
I sacrificed my Dark Magician to finish Yugi.

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:02.240
But it failed.

00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:10.110
Please wait just a little longer.

00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:15.970
Well, it's still good that I got rid of his Dark Magician.

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:21.480
I still have two more Dark Magicians in my deck.

00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:24.680
Continue the duel!

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:26.960
It's my End Phase.

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:31.700
I set a card and end my turn.

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:39.710
Yugi, I know that there are no other Dark Magicians in your deck.

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:45.940
It's definite that I'll be the one known as the true Dark Magician user.

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:48.460
We'll see about that, Pandora.

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:51.140
If you're a true Dark Magician user...

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:57.960
...you should be able to hear your cards grieving for being betrayed by their master and sacrificed!

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:00.480
I don't hear that.

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:03.460
But I do hear a pleasant sound.

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:10.550
The sound of a buzzsaw waiting to chop you up!

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:15.800
Yugi, you only have 700 life points left.

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:20.320
When it reaches 0, the buzzsaw will slice you.

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:26.480
And my great escape show will end perfectly.

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:30.760
Only the cards know how this battle will end!

00:03:31.130 --> 00:03:33.000
Here I go!  My turn!

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:37.900
Pandora doesn't have any monsters on his field.

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:40.030
This is my chance to attack!

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:47.710
I summon Gazelle the King of Mythical Beasts!

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:52.960
You fell into my trap.

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:56.060
The trap card Shadow Balance!

00:03:57.940 --> 00:03:58.780
What?

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:03.250
This trap card activates when you summon a monster.

00:04:03.250 --> 00:04:09.000
You will lose monsters until you have the same amount as I do.

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:13.880
Oh no!

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:16.800
He has zero monsters on his field, so...

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:19.570
That's right!  Balance's Judgment!

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:36.080
My monsters...

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:41.400
Now we both have zero monsters.

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:45.100
After you went through all the trouble of summoning a monster.

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:46.800
My turn.

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:52.640
With this card, I'm guaranteed to win.

00:04:53.050 --> 00:05:00.220
Since we both don't have any monsters, whoever summons a high Level monster first will win.

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:05.680
Yugi, my strategy has already overwhelmed you.

00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:12.660
Because I have a card that lets me instantly summon a high Level monster.

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:17.670
A card that lets me summon the greatest magician, Dark Magician!

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:20.370
A quick summoning card?

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:22.170
Here I go!

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:24.660
This is my key card to victory!

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:28.580
Dark Magic Curtain!

00:05:34.510 --> 00:05:43.140
Each player can pay half his life points to summon a Dark Magician from his deck this turn.

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:47.220
Come, Dark Magician!

00:05:57.070 --> 00:06:01.110
Yugi, how do you like my perfect magician deck?

00:06:01.110 --> 00:06:09.520
Its combination of summoning speed, quickness and magic outperforms yours in every way.

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:16.450
You must admit that I'm the true Dark Magician user.

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:23.160
You have no monsters on your field.

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:29.460
If I attack with Dark Magician this turn, you will run out of life points, and I win.

00:06:29.770 --> 00:06:33.940
Your only hope is your set cards.

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:40.420
They're probably trap cards that will destroy my monster when I attack.

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:44.950
They're eyesores, so I'll seal those set cards away.

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:47.150
Seal away set cards?

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:49.800
The spell card Anti-Magic Arrows!

00:06:55.160 --> 00:06:58.570
I've sealed away all your countermeasures.

00:06:58.570 --> 00:06:59.900
You lose.

00:07:02.050 --> 00:07:05.250
Dark Magician, attack him directly!

00:07:08.350 --> 00:07:09.240
I win.

00:07:15.530 --> 00:07:16.380
What?

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:20.520
Dark Magic Curtain is on Yugi's field?

00:07:20.650 --> 00:07:27.520
Yes.  Your spell card Dark Magic Curtain affects the entire field.

00:07:29.140 --> 00:07:33.230
That means I can also use the spell.

00:07:34.250 --> 00:07:38.380
I've also summoned a magician card!

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:43.900
Impossible!  You don't have another Dark Magician in your deck!

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:47.340
You're right.  I only have one Dark Magician in my deck.

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:49.450
Then who is it?

00:07:49.750 --> 00:07:57.950
In the world of Duel Monsters, there's one student who has received the magic of the mightiest magician.

00:07:58.200 --> 00:07:59.400
No way!

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:03.690
There's a card that a Magician user like me doesn't know?

00:08:03.820 --> 00:08:05.200
I'll show you!

00:08:21.770 --> 00:08:23.800
Dark Magician Girl!

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:27.050
Dark Magician Girl?

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:33.890
But Dark Magician Girl has 2000 attack points.

00:08:33.890 --> 00:08:37.650
Dark Magician has enough attack points to take her down!

00:08:37.650 --> 00:08:41.060
Dark Magician, attack Dark Magician Girl!

00:08:44.850 --> 00:08:46.120
Black Magic!

00:08:46.120 --> 00:08:47.820
Black Burning!

00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:53.080
Now I win!

00:08:53.350 --> 00:08:55.000
Are you sure about that?

00:09:07.470 --> 00:09:11.560
No way!  My Dark Magician is vanishing...

00:09:12.050 --> 00:09:16.930
Why?  It had 500 more attack points than your monster.

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:18.650
I'll tell you why.

00:09:18.650 --> 00:09:26.600
Dark Magician Girl gains 300 attack points for every Dark Magician in the graveyard.

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:30.440
The student inherits her master's soul and becomes stronger!

00:09:30.450 --> 00:09:31.950
But...

00:09:32.990 --> 00:09:37.000
There's only one Dark Magician in Yugi's graveyard.

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:43.200
Even with 300 more points, it'll only have 2300 attack points, so my Dark Magician is still stronger!

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:44.900
Look closer.

00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:49.170
If you're a Dark Magician user, you should be able to see the truth.

00:09:57.730 --> 00:09:58.910
There's another one.

00:10:01.880 --> 00:10:03.080
No way!

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:07.240
It also inherited the soul of my Dark Magician?

00:10:07.240 --> 00:10:12.920
Dark Magician Girl inherits the souls of Dark Magicians in every graveyard.

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:20.680
Including the grieving soul of the Dark Magician that you betrayed.

00:10:23.500 --> 00:10:24.930
My turn!

00:10:25.180 --> 00:10:27.150
Prepare yourself, Pandora!

00:10:42.960 --> 00:10:48.040
Dark Magician Girl, attack Pandora directly!

00:10:59.500 --> 00:11:01.290
Black Burning!

00:11:04.360 --> 00:11:08.150
You betrayed your cards' trust and lost, Pandora!

00:11:15.370 --> 00:11:17.390
Hey, guys!  What are you doing?

00:11:17.890 --> 00:11:20.390
Honda!  Yugi is missing!

00:11:20.600 --> 00:11:21.420
What?

00:11:21.880 --> 00:11:24.630
The Ghouls must have took him.

00:11:24.820 --> 00:11:27.870
My brother thinks he's in the basement of this store.

00:11:28.360 --> 00:11:31.900
Since we know where he is, let's barge in!

00:11:33.750 --> 00:11:39.100
When a duelist breaks his bond with his cards, he falls into a pit of defeat.

00:11:39.440 --> 00:11:43.150
You lost because your own Dark Magician wanted revenge!

00:11:43.460 --> 00:11:48.100
Impossible...  A duelist controls his cards.

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:52.650
A card can't act on its own and want revenge against its master!

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:58.520
You sliced your cards to cheat, so you sliced away your cards' souls to win!

00:11:58.520 --> 00:12:02.400
You don't have the soul of a duelist!

00:12:03.500 --> 00:12:07.640
Pandora, your own cruel ritual awaits you.

00:12:09.050 --> 00:12:11.280
I almost forgot!

00:12:11.970 --> 00:12:16.880
The buzzsaw will pass the zero marker and cut me up!

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:19.380
Stay away!

00:12:22.460 --> 00:12:24.310
A key and a Puzzle Card!

00:12:30.050 --> 00:12:31.110
He's here?

00:12:33.970 --> 00:12:36.030
What's that noise?

00:12:38.890 --> 00:12:40.400
I'm done for!

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:41.450
Just kidding.

00:12:41.450 --> 00:12:43.650
Never underestimate an illusionist.

00:12:43.650 --> 00:12:48.120
Just in case, I hid a spare key in my sleeve.

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:54.110
With this, I can easily escape.

00:12:54.550 --> 00:12:57.020
Huh?  What's going on?

00:12:57.020 --> 00:12:59.350
I can't move my fingers.

00:13:00.270 --> 00:13:01.060
Pandora.

00:13:02.740 --> 00:13:03.890
Marik...

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:08.300
You lost the duel, so you must face the consequences.

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:12.560
Save me!  Forgive me, Marik!

00:13:17.260 --> 00:13:23.200
Huh?  I thought I had the key in my hand, but it's gone!

00:13:23.600 --> 00:13:26.230
I control your memories.

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:30.140
I erased the memories you had of that key.

00:13:30.140 --> 00:13:33.050
You will never see the key again.

00:13:40.520 --> 00:13:41.870
Yugi!

00:13:41.870 --> 00:13:42.900
Are you there?

00:13:43.270 --> 00:13:44.640
Answer if you are!

00:13:49.980 --> 00:13:50.900
Watch out!

00:14:00.370 --> 00:14:03.520
Losing your life in a game is wrong!

00:14:07.380 --> 00:14:09.020
Catherine...

00:14:09.450 --> 00:14:11.420
Catherine!

00:14:11.420 --> 00:14:13.140
Catherine!

00:14:16.850 --> 00:14:22.420
Catherine, never leave my side again.

00:14:24.220 --> 00:14:27.540
Catherine...

00:14:27.940 --> 00:14:32.280
I'm sorry I hurt you because I didn't know how you felt.

00:14:32.770 --> 00:14:34.970
I don't need money or fame.

00:14:34.970 --> 00:14:38.000
Let's go back to France and start over.

00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:41.290
What's going on?

00:14:41.820 --> 00:14:43.080
Pandora?

00:14:45.140 --> 00:14:46.970
Don't interfere.

00:14:47.910 --> 00:14:52.030
You must be the other Yugi, the present-day vessel for the soul.

00:14:52.370 --> 00:14:54.300
His personality has changed.

00:14:54.300 --> 00:14:55.040
Who are you?

00:14:55.570 --> 00:14:59.620
Oh yeah.  I didn't tell the vessel my name yet.

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:02.040
My name is Marik.

00:15:02.370 --> 00:15:03.280
Marik?

00:15:04.120 --> 00:15:08.150
I can control people from a distance.

00:15:08.570 --> 00:15:12.920
By controlling his memories, I'm able to see and hear.

00:15:13.290 --> 00:15:16.290
So I can see and hear you.

00:15:16.290 --> 00:15:19.030
I controlled Keith the same way.

00:15:19.900 --> 00:15:21.000
Back then?

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:26.910
Yes.  In order to determine the identity of your other self.

00:15:27.470 --> 00:15:33.540
If the Millennium Puzzle actually chose you, then he would be inside you.

00:15:33.540 --> 00:15:39.390
And by completing the Millennium Puzzle, you revealed his identity to me.

00:15:40.560 --> 00:15:43.720
Why do you want to kill us?  Answer me!

00:15:43.950 --> 00:15:46.620
I‘m not interested in you.

00:15:46.620 --> 00:15:49.230
I'm after the soul inside the vessel!

00:15:50.240 --> 00:15:51.390
Revenge.

00:15:52.010 --> 00:15:55.850
The family of gravekeepers has lived in the shadows for 3,000 years.

00:15:55.850 --> 00:15:57.720
Their descendants want revenge!

00:15:58.510 --> 00:16:01.240
Revenge?  Gravekeepers?

00:16:02.080 --> 00:16:09.560
In Egypt's remote region of Necropolis, to protect the lost Pharaoh's secrets...

00:16:09.560 --> 00:16:13.160
...we couldn't have any contact with the outside world, so we had no freedom.

00:16:13.160 --> 00:16:17.480
We, the gravekeepers, lived in the shadows.

00:16:18.320 --> 00:16:25.940
Since ancient times, my family was destined to protect the Valley of the Kings and the Millennium Items.

00:16:25.940 --> 00:16:27.160
And then...

00:16:28.320 --> 00:16:31.160
Everyone died obeying their destiny.

00:16:31.540 --> 00:16:36.680
Their duty was to return the Pharaoh's memories when he resurrected.

00:16:37.160 --> 00:16:38.600
Memories?

00:16:38.600 --> 00:16:44.400
Do you have anything to do with the seven Items that must be placed in the tablet of the Pharaoh's memories?

00:16:44.550 --> 00:16:48.440
Yes.  I have one of those Items.

00:16:48.820 --> 00:16:54.330
I must protect it with my life until I can present it to the Pharaoh's soul.

00:16:54.330 --> 00:16:57.200
That was taught to me since I was young.

00:16:57.200 --> 00:17:01.060
The question is: Where is the Pharaoh's soul?

00:17:01.260 --> 00:17:08.200
The best way to find out is written in the ancient Egyptian text Prt M Hrw.

00:17:08.680 --> 00:17:12.550
It says the three God Cards will point to the Pharaoh.

00:17:12.930 --> 00:17:18.170
So the one who gathers the three God Cards will become the Pharaoh.

00:17:18.170 --> 00:17:22.450
He will have the seven Millennium Items and regain the lost memories.

00:17:22.620 --> 00:17:24.550
Three God Cards?

00:17:24.920 --> 00:17:26.690
The lost memories!

00:17:27.470 --> 00:17:33.930
My family has sacrificed much to protect the Millennium Items, including my father.

00:17:34.240 --> 00:17:42.440
To end our cursed destiny, I must get revenge on the Pharaoh's soul and kill him again.

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:46.440
And if the God Cards point to the Pharaoh...

00:17:47.960 --> 00:17:52.450
I will become the new Pharaoh when I acquire all the cards!

00:17:52.450 --> 00:17:53.950
The new Pharaoh?

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:59.450
I formed the Ghouls to find the three God Cards.

00:17:59.850 --> 00:18:02.440
I've acquired two of them.

00:18:02.440 --> 00:18:04.890
The final card is in this city.

00:18:05.820 --> 00:18:07.460
In Battle City!

00:18:08.870 --> 00:18:15.450
I now know what my other self is fighting for in this city.

00:18:15.770 --> 00:18:17.700
It's for his lost memories!

00:18:18.110 --> 00:18:27.950
If I acquire the three God Cards and kill you, I'll be freed from my curse of destiny and rule everything!

00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:35.280
If I don't get the God Cards or his lost memories, my other self will never leave me.

00:18:35.280 --> 00:18:42.920
But my other self really wants his precious memories back.

00:18:43.800 --> 00:18:50.150
We can head towards the future because we're building on the memories of the past.

00:18:50.320 --> 00:18:55.600
But since my other self doesn't know his past, he's standing still.

00:18:55.960 --> 00:18:58.810
There's nothing sadder than that.

00:18:59.160 --> 00:19:07.820
Even if regaining his memories means that we'll have to go our separate ways, we still have to try.

00:19:08.240 --> 00:19:09.050
Marik!

00:19:09.530 --> 00:19:12.840
I won't let you kill my other self!

00:19:12.840 --> 00:19:14.080
We will fight!

00:19:15.160 --> 00:19:17.900
Big talk from a mere vessel.

00:19:18.270 --> 00:19:20.570
You will die too.

00:19:22.350 --> 00:19:26.200
A Rare Hunter with a God Card is already in this city.

00:19:27.370 --> 00:19:30.080
He has Slifer the Sky Dragon.

00:19:31.020 --> 00:19:33.080
Slifer the Sky Dragon?

00:19:33.370 --> 00:19:35.810
He'll eventually appear before you.

00:19:36.070 --> 00:19:38.820
Beware of the silent puppet.

00:19:40.520 --> 00:19:42.350
Silent puppet?

00:19:42.670 --> 00:19:44.900
We'll meet again, Yugi.

00:19:51.100 --> 00:19:55.210
We'll fight to regain his lost memories!

00:19:57.130 --> 00:19:58.960
Are you okay, Yugi?

00:19:58.960 --> 00:19:59.770
Yugi!

00:20:00.320 --> 00:20:01.260
Everyone!

00:20:01.690 --> 00:20:02.780
Thank goodness!

00:20:02.780 --> 00:20:04.300
I was so worried!

00:20:05.400 --> 00:20:06.940
Just wait.

00:20:06.940 --> 00:20:11.780
I'll bury you and your annoying vessel into the darkness.

00:20:11.960 --> 00:20:14.440
What about the God Cards?

00:20:14.440 --> 00:20:17.580
A God Card requires a God Card.

00:20:17.580 --> 00:20:22.540
I'll go to Domino City with my Ra card.

00:20:23.760 --> 00:20:26.520
You're going to fight Kaiba yourself?

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:29.320
That time will come eventually.

00:20:29.530 --> 00:20:35.760
For now, monitor Yugi and his entourage and don't lose sight of them.

00:20:35.920 --> 00:20:36.540
Okay.

00:20:36.820 --> 00:20:39.040
He's going to entertain me.

00:20:39.560 --> 00:20:46.550
Marik only says "entertain" when he's talking about people he despises.

00:20:49.180 --> 00:20:54.860
Acquiring the third God Card should be the Ghouls' highest priority.

00:20:54.860 --> 00:20:57.870
However, Marik is after Yugi.

00:21:11.600 --> 00:21:12.880
The Ra card.

00:21:13.870 --> 00:21:17.520
Yugi, I'll be the one to crush you!

00:21:19.940 --> 00:21:23.870
I swear upon these hated carvings that I will defeat you!

00:21:24.400 --> 00:21:27.340
Sister, I won't forgive him.

00:21:27.660 --> 00:21:32.640
Yugi killed our family and our father!

00:21:41.310 --> 00:21:44.000
A fan asks Jonouchi for his autograph.

00:21:44.000 --> 00:21:48.170
While you're caught up in the moment, he steals your Duel Disk!

00:21:48.310 --> 00:21:51.110
He manages to get his Duel Disk back...

00:21:51.110 --> 00:21:54.860
...but the kid says Insector Haga threatened him and took his rare cards!

00:21:54.860 --> 00:21:58.570
Jonouchi is angry and challenges Haga to a duel.

00:21:58.570 --> 00:22:01.860
Wait a sec!  I didn't know you had that card!

00:22:02.150 --> 00:22:05.750
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Revenge Trap
Out of Control!  Paracide

00:22:05.930 --> 00:22:07.340
Duel, standby!

00:22:21.930 --> 00:22:26.430
Even a long, long time ago

00:22:27.230 --> 00:22:31.800
I feel like I've been here

00:22:32.340 --> 00:22:41.480
The setting sun colors the classroom after school

00:22:41.780 --> 00:22:52.990
We all laugh as you point out that I cut my bangs too short

00:22:55.860 --> 00:23:00.500
Time passes bit by bit

00:23:01.170 --> 00:23:05.770
The time when my bangs touch my eyelids

00:23:06.340 --> 00:23:10.880
Will never change

00:23:11.540 --> 00:23:16.150
The sunset envelops everyone

00:23:16.780 --> 00:23:21.350
To be who I am

00:23:21.950 --> 00:23:26.590
I've kept searching for something

00:23:27.260 --> 00:23:31.300
The time that we're now spending together

00:23:31.300 --> 00:23:34.230
I learned that's the answer

00:23:35.030 --> 00:23:41.340
From now until forever...
